<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Criollo people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as creole</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Criollos, or creoles, were people of Spanish descent born in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> during the colonial period. They formed much of the colonial elite but were often excluded from the highest offices in favour of Spanish-born officials. Their resentment, sharpened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bourbon-reforms">Bourbon Reforms</a>, fuelled the independence movements that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> in the Americas.</p></div>
